{"id": "gc-indi-76232e61", "d": "add", "leaf": "P1.1.1/2", "page": "1:21:0", "mcq": {"s": "\"Thy right is to work only, but never with its fruits.\" This is stated in which of the following texts?", "o": ["Ashtadhyayi", "Mahabhashya", "Bhagavad Gita", "Ramayana"], "a": 2, "x": "The line 'karmanye vadhikaraste ma phaleshu kadachana' is from the Bhagavad Gita (Chapter 2), Krishna's teaching of nishkama karma to Arjuna. The Ashtadhyayi is Panini's grammar and the Mahabhashya is Patanjali's commentary on it.", "src": "UPPSC (Pre) 1992"}}
